A previously mentioned spoiler you may have missed:



A number of potions have an effect while being wielded and can thus be
identified without any harm:

 blindness, hallucination, confusion, levitation, invisibility,
 ?sickness/poison

And even if they are "cursed", they can always be un-wielded and stop
having their effect at that time.

This can be useful for more than identification.  For example
blindness can be used as a blindfold, except that you can't wield a
weapon at the same time.  Levitation and invisibilty can be used
similarly.  And you may occaisionally wish to wield a potion of
confusion while reading some scrolls.


